course: dictionary
lesson: 1597
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «At the checkout, the cashier scanned every item.» The words scanned and cashier tell you checkout is the place in a shop where you pay.
explain: Checkout can also be a page on a website, where you pay for your order. «Ask an adult before you enter your card at the online checkout.» Online and card are the clues, so this meaning is about a website.
explain: In a hotel, checkout is the time you must leave your room. «Checkout is at eleven, so pack your bags early.» The clock time is the clue. Check out, with two words, is a phrase for leaving: «We check out of the hotel at noon.»
fact: Checkout is a noun: a checkout, checkouts. You can say «at the checkout».
fact: «Checkout» means the place in a shop or supermarket where you pay for things.
fact: «Checkout» can also mean the page on a website where you pay for your order.
fact: «Checkout» can mean the time you must leave a hotel room.
fact: Check out, two words, is a phrase: «We check out of the hotel at noon.»
exercise: «At the checkout, the cashier scanned every item.» Where is the checkout here? | In a hotel, where you sleep | At school, in the library | *In a shop, where you pay | On a bus, by the driver
exercise: «Please pay at the checkout on the website before your order is sent.» What does checkout mean? | A bag for shopping | *A page on a website where you pay | A hotel room key | A shop till with a long queue
exercise: «Checkout is at eleven, so we must leave our room by then.» What does checkout mean here? | A machine that counts coins | *The time you must leave a hotel room | A place where you pay for food | A short walk to the shops
test: Which meaning fits? «The self-checkout beeped because I had not scanned an item.» | A mountain path with loose stones | A type of bread | A hotel room with a view | *A machine in a shop where you scan and pay yourself
test: Ella is lost in a big shop. Where should she go to get help? | *To a checkout, to tell a staff member | To the vending machine, and wait there | To the car park, to wait alone | To the shop door, and walk outside by herself
exam: In «We check out of the hotel at noon», what does check out mean? | *To leave the hotel | To count the money in a till | To sleep in a tent | To buy a new coat
